gm-method: when a code comment claims a cross-system bridge/consumer already exists (e.g. "shader X already consumes this uniform"), verify with an exhaustive grep for the claimed function/uniform name before building on that assumption -- a comment can describe an intended design that was never actually finished on the receiving end. A silently-dropped extra function argument (caller passes N args, callee signature only declares N-1) is a common, easy-to-miss version of this: no error is thrown, the argument is just unused, and the feature "half-works" (renders correctly, just missing the one signal that never arrives).